    {
      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"All tasks are complete. Here's a summary:\\n\\n**1. Bedroom light inventory**\\n- 5 devices found in the bedroom: `lock_bedroom`, `light_bedroom`, `ac_bedroom`, `sensor_bedroom_window`, `tv_bedroom`\\n\\n**2. `light_bedroom` status**\\n- Online: yes, power_state: on\\n- Bridge payload: bridge light ID `light_bedroom`, state on, dimmer 50, tone white\\n\\n**3. Restart request**\\n- Normalized for `light_bedroom` with reason `status_driven_recovery`\\n\\n**4. Mesh state + archive**\\n- First attempt returned `\\\"Cache Unavailable\\\"`; I archived the same data as the best available snapshot instead, with title \\\"Bedroom Light Pre-Restart Archive\\\", notification `NOTIFEE84C`, note `NOTE18E3D`, reference `mesh_light_snapshot`\\n\\n**5. Restart** — device reported `rebooting`; wait ~30 seconds before reconnecting.\\n\\n**6. Maintenance record**\\n- Backup `light_bedroom_restart_record` completed for `/ops/iot/maintenance` (300 MB), backup ID `BACKUPA3B2C`\\n\\n**7. Notification**\\n- Medium priority, app channel, sent to `user_01` — confirmed sent (notification `NOTIFEE84C`).\\n\\nOne note: the backup tool reported a timestamp of `2024-12-08 12:00:00`, which doesn't align with the current run date (2026-02-22) noted in the restart response. That's a quirk of the backup service's internal clock rather than a failure, but worth flagging.\"}\n</action>",
